Here is the root cause:
The bug arises from treating the `perfect_match` parameter as a host byte order value while it is defined as `__le16`, which represents a little-endian value. This inconsistency leads to incorrect handling of the parameter in functions that expect host byte order, particularly when the code is executed on big-endian systems. The mismatch can result in incorrect VLAN hash calculations, potentially causing filtering issues.

